@startuml

' High-level layering of ImgLabs: each layer depends only on the one beneath it
' UI drives image compute, which composes GPU work through the Kernel Engine,
' which ultimately dispatches the raw Metal shader functions

title ImgLabs — High-Level Layers

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false

component "SwiftUI UI\n(ContentView, DuplicateView)" as UI
component "Image Compute\n(ImageCorrelation, DuplicateFinder)" as Compute
component "Kernel Engine\n(MetalComputeContext, MetalRunner)" as Engine
component "Metal Shaders\n(ImgMath.metal, ArrayMath.metal)" as Shaders

UI --> Compute : import / analyze
Compute --> Engine : build & run kernels
Engine --> Shaders : dispatch on GPU

@enduml
